{"kind":"event","event_id":2063,"event_uid":"01M2HDX0JMR9P9S6Z9XTY6QH1B","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.metadata_updated","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":119,"issue_uid":"01M2HDVKBR9NSQBG2WTXG8SWH2","issue_short_id":"swh2","actor":"exam:1@run-133","hlc_physical_ms":1789438886484,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"98f46a7b06b53c985404d0c0328bb653d44ef6678c6c476f78ec1c13e32fb46e","payload":{"diff":{"work.attention":{"from":null,"to":"ok"}},"revision_new":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-15T02:21:26.483Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T02:21:26.484Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":2064,"event_uid":"01M2HDXK4CWE9SCK1Y5Q2N8X1Y","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":119,"issue_uid":"01M2HDVKBR9NSQBG2WTXG8SWH2","issue_short_id":"swh2","actor":"impl:1@run-133","hlc_physical_ms":1789438905484,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"227221db0d2f97ed54dfc25b6b407eebd74885558e9072d0149cbeb9cf35a9cb","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HDXK4B0FPG3X432X3QZF6C","author":"impl:1@run-133","body":"Task 1 (ready-set scheduler) starting. Plan: replace the WAVES-barrier loop in fleet/run-engine.mjs with W lanes handed to `parallel` as W thunks; readiness computed from the store at read time (not dispatched, not failed, not blockedByDep, all EDGES predecessors adopted); each lane re-anchors its clone at the current adopted head per dispatch, and on return folds every captured-unadopted mergeable under one fold lock as the next epoch via foldWave. Epochs number from 1 and keep the driver:wave-adopted / driver:wave-blocked event names. Deleting CONCURRENCY, waveLabel, waveIds and the barrier retry loop; parked-infra retried once on a slot free.","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:21:45.483201245Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T02:21:45.484Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":2065,"event_uid":"01M2HE4GRX187B63CPMTWM1X12","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":119,"issue_uid":"01M2HDVKBR9NSQBG2WTXG8SWH2","issue_short_id":"swh2","actor":"exam:1@run-133","hlc_physical_ms":1789439132445,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"c870b7570cb5af265255b536cd6a02bb444027c961c05ae9f4b954f769e17105","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HE4GRVM3GDFH98FA9BDZT3","author":"exam:1@run-133","body":"Examiner (exam for Task 1), approach before writing:\n\nThe exam is one sim on the run-engine rig (`_engine_helpers.mjs`), `fleet/tests/test_run_engine_ready_set.mjs`, legs (a)–(e) plus in-file copies of (f) and (h). (g) is carried by its `Run:` lines alone — the hermetic guard forbids a sim naming a sibling sim, so the eight sims are never spelled here.\n\nReadings I am fixing now, so a later session does not have to re-derive them:\n\n- **The ordered log.** The rig does not run `run-worker.mjs`, so no `worker:start`/`worker:end` reaches `events.jsonl` on its own. The exam's stub appends them itself, in production's order (start on entry, end just before returning), to the same `<runDir>/events.jsonl` the engine appends its `driver:*` events to. That one file is the total order every ordering leg reads. Sim-only synchronisation uses marker files beside it, never a new event kind.\n- **Holds are bounded.** Every `wait until X is on the log` in a stub times out (8 s) and returns, so at BASE — where the fold happens only at the wave barrier — the sim fails an assertion naming the absent scheduler instead of hanging. That is the price of the exam being runnable at BASE at all.\n- **Width.** `extraArgs: {width: n}`; `args.width` is unread at BASE, so BASE dispatches the whole wave in one `CONCURRENCY` chunk and the width legs are red there.\n- **Fold serialisation (c)** is read off a wrapped `exec`: every `python3 <KERNEL> <verb>` call is recorded begin/end. Two rules — never two kernel calls in flight at once, and no second `fold` begins between a `fold` and the first `materialize` that ends after it. The same wrapper is the gate that holds the first `fold` for leg (c)'s X/Y/Z scenario.\n- **The red epoch in (d)** is a `check.sh` that exits non-zero, printing nothing, once B's file exists: an output naming no path is NOT the unattributed-red route (`failingTestPaths` returns []), so it takes the reconcile route, and the stub answers `reconcile:wave<n>:1` with a non-FIXED status — one dispatch, then `TEST_FAILED`.\n- **The infra death in (e)** is the implementer returning `null` once (`AGENT_NULL` → `parked-infra`), with the `worker:end` `{class:'infra',status}` line appended first, as production orders it.\n- **Legs (f)/(h) are duplicated in-file** with exactly the semantics of their `Run:` lines (a zero count of the four strings in `run-engine.mjs`; the five words in order inside the CONTRACT bullet from `The engine's own wave record` to `driver:exam-run`), so the exam grades them too rather than only the driver's shell.","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:25:32.443816200Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T02:25:32.445Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":2066,"event_uid":"01M2HEV1F8D1K71SH23VE8SHY7","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":119,"issue_uid":"01M2HDVKBR9NSQBG2WTXG8SWH2","issue_short_id":"swh2","actor":"exam:1@run-133","hlc_physical_ms":1789439870440,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"d5c879510ea7601bf112e104c68ceae4998979608ad0fe72d2dd46d4196f0e7e","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HEV1F7V1M6M59TENKXBTAD","author":"exam:1@run-133","body":"Exam for task 1 (ready set + epochs) is written at fleet/tests/test_run_engine_ready_set.mjs and red at BASE, dying at (a)/M2 with driver:wave-adopted listing [\"A\",\"B\",\"C\"] — the wave barrier, which is exactly the absent implementation.\n\nOne reading a later session would otherwise have to rediscover: leg (c) holds the kernel's FIRST fold until Y's and Z's REFEREE envelopes are on the log (worker:end review:<id>:*), not merely the implementers'. A task's result is only captured and pending after its review returns and its patch is taken, so gating on worker:end impl:Y/Z could let epoch 1 finish while Y and Z were not yet foldable — a correct engine would then legitimately produce three epochs and the exam would fail it for nothing. Every canned dispatch (impl, review, reconcile) therefore mirrors production's worker:start/worker:end into the same events.jsonl, which is also the one total order all the ordering legs read; only impl starts carry 'head', since judgments run in the integration clone.\n\nLeg (g) (the eight sims print ALL TESTS PASSED) is carried by its Run: lines alone — the hermetic probe forbids a sim naming a sibling sim, so those names appear nowhere in the file. Legs (f) and (h) are also duplicated in-file as live string/order checks over run-engine.mjs and CONTRACT.md.","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:37:50.439547264Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T02:37:50.44Z"}
